{
  "about": "Test list for the AI theme check (plan doc: Choosing the model). Run with scripts/ai-test.mjs. expected: ok | inappropriate | either (reasonable teachers could disagree; any verdict counts) | ok_or_unknown (clean but recent or obscure: the model may not know it). The rules got stricter in prompt v2: any drug reference, drinking as the main theme and even mild sexual innuendo are inappropriate, and clean or radio edits are judged by the original song. group a = inappropriate for school but not marked explicit, or with a clean version; b = innocent songs with alarming titles; c = clean popular, recent and obscure songs; group d = Instrumentals only (prompt v5): instrumental = true when nobody sings or raps in the recording, false when someone does; graded separately. group e = songs released 2024-2026, past the model's knowledge (it mostly answers UNKNOWN): the test of judging from LRCLIB lyrics (scripts/ai-test.mjs --group e --lyrics; src/lyrics.js). group g (2026-10-22, Dalton: most complaints are mild songs that SEEM inappropriate, e.g. Bruno Mars) = mild songs the live verdict cache blocked, expected OK, next to the same artists' songs that really are not for class (must stay inappropriate). v7 (2026-10-23, Dalton): ANY alcohol, drugs (metaphors too) or smoking/vaping blocks, even one passing line. group h (2026-10-23) = a held-out check of v7 on songs the prompt was never tuned on: one passing line of alcohol, drugs, smoking or sex next to clean school favourites. group i (2026-10-23) = not music for class: meme, noise and sound tracks the word list cannot see, next to real instrumental music that must stay OK. group k (2026-10-24) = political and troll picks (the teachers' own bans) next to real songs whose titles must not be read as trolling.",
